MTD	mzTab-version	2.1.0-M
MTD	mzTab-ID	ST001339_AN002233
MTD	mzTab-profile	M+S
MTD	title	Disruption of Redox Balance Enhances the Effects of BRAF-inhibitors in Melanoma
MTD	description	Specifically, we report that drug-insensitive melanoma cells can maintain higher levels of antioxidant metabolites to withstand the lethal effects of drugs. By extending our analysis to other melanoma subtypes in the TCGA, we show that elevated redox capacity could indeed be a general feature of melanoma. Our results suggest that redox vulnerabilities could be exploited for therapeutic benefits and identify unsuspected combination targets to enhance the effects of BRAFi in pan-melanoma.
